1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:03,250
This is Logos Forum,

2
00:00:03,250 --> 00:00:06,450
a forum that runs inside Logos Basecamp,

3
00:00:06,450 --> 00:00:08,950
with no server anywhere.

4
00:00:08,950 --> 00:00:12,150
Topics and replies travel peer to peer

5
00:00:12,150 --> 00:00:13,950
over Logos Messaging,

6
00:00:13,950 --> 00:00:16,350
history is kept on each device

7
00:00:16,350 --> 00:00:19,150
and shared through Logos Storage,

8
00:00:19,150 --> 00:00:22,400
and every single post is signed.

9
00:00:22,950 --> 00:00:25,450
The check mark means

10
00:00:25,450 --> 00:00:28,750
this app verifies the signature itself.

11
00:00:28,750 --> 00:00:32,250
It does not trust anyone to tell it.

12
00:00:33,233 --> 00:00:36,233
Installing it takes one link.

13
00:00:36,233 --> 00:00:37,633
In Basecamp settings,

14
00:00:37,633 --> 00:00:40,333
add the forum's package repository,

15
00:00:40,333 --> 00:00:42,033
open the Package Manager

16
00:00:42,033 --> 00:00:44,433
and install Logos Forum.

17
00:00:45,233 --> 00:00:47,833
Basecamp pulls in Logos Messaging

18
00:00:47,833 --> 00:00:49,933
and Logos Storage with it.

19
00:00:49,933 --> 00:00:52,083
That's the whole setup.

20
00:00:55,867 --> 00:01:00,567
Now, two real nodes on the Logos test network.

21
00:01:00,567 --> 00:01:03,967
Alice on the left, Bob on the right.

22
00:01:03,967 --> 00:01:06,967
No shared server between them.

23
00:01:06,967 --> 00:01:11,167
Alice asks when testnet 0.3 lands,

24
00:01:11,167 --> 00:01:14,767
and a moment later it shows up on Bob's side,

25
00:01:14,767 --> 00:01:16,417
already verified.

26
00:01:18,733 --> 00:01:22,033
Bob answers under an alias,

27
00:01:22,033 --> 00:01:23,933
Ghost for example.

28
00:01:23,933 --> 00:01:25,833
People see the name he picked,

29
00:01:25,833 --> 00:01:28,983
but the post is still signed by his key,

30
00:01:29,583 --> 00:01:33,733
and it is clearly marked as an alias.

31
00:01:35,300 --> 00:01:37,900
Alice replies anonymously.

32
00:01:37,900 --> 00:01:41,900
The app makes a key for that one post,

33
00:01:41,900 --> 00:01:44,700
signs with it and throws it away.

34
00:01:44,700 --> 00:01:46,500
Two anonymous posts can't be linked

35
00:01:46,500 --> 00:01:49,050
to each other or back to her.

36
00:01:50,567 --> 00:01:53,167
She can also rotate her key.

37
00:01:53,167 --> 00:01:54,967
One click, a brand new key,

38
00:01:54,967 --> 00:01:58,467
and nothing links it to the old one.

39
00:01:58,467 --> 00:01:59,967
Look at Bob's side:

40
00:01:59,967 --> 00:02:02,267
her earlier posts and her new one

41
00:02:02,267 --> 00:02:04,617
show two unrelated keys.

42
00:02:07,967 --> 00:02:11,767
Bob loses his connection, on a train say.

43
00:02:11,767 --> 00:02:14,367
He still writes his reply.

44
00:02:14,367 --> 00:02:18,267
It's saved on his device and marked as waiting,

45
00:02:18,267 --> 00:02:21,467
and it reaches no one yet.

46
00:02:21,467 --> 00:02:23,267
The moment he's back online,

47
00:02:23,267 --> 00:02:25,667
it goes out on its own,

48
00:02:25,667 --> 00:02:27,617
and Alice gets it.

49
00:02:29,167 --> 00:02:31,167
A brand new user joins,

50
00:02:31,167 --> 00:02:33,067
with nothing on their machine.

51
00:02:33,067 --> 00:02:35,967
They ask the peers already there

52
00:02:35,967 --> 00:02:37,767
and receive the whole history,

53
00:02:37,767 --> 00:02:39,767
every topic and every reply.

54
00:02:39,767 --> 00:02:42,717
Each one checked again on arrival.

55
00:02:44,133 --> 00:02:46,833
The interface adapts to any width,

56
00:02:47,483 --> 00:02:51,333
from a wide desktop down to a phone.

57
00:02:51,333 --> 00:02:53,233
One pane at a time,

58
00:02:53,233 --> 00:02:54,633
nothing cut off,

59
00:02:54,633 --> 00:02:57,083
nothing pushed off the screen.

60
00:02:58,633 --> 00:03:01,933
All of this is tested.

61
00:03:01,933 --> 00:03:04,133
Thirty core tests

62
00:03:04,133 --> 00:03:08,633
and a full end-to-end run on the real network.

63
00:03:08,633 --> 00:03:11,033
Five nodes, 24 checks,

64
00:03:11,033 --> 00:03:14,833
aliases, anonymous posts, rotation, offline,

65
00:03:14,833 --> 00:03:17,533
and history for newcomers.

66
00:03:18,133 --> 00:03:22,833
CI builds it for macOS and Linux

67
00:03:22,833 --> 00:03:24,683
on every commit.

68
00:03:27,267 --> 00:03:30,067
So this is Logos Forum.

69
00:03:30,067 --> 00:03:32,067
No server, signed posts,

70
00:03:32,067 --> 00:03:34,867
and privacy you choose, post by post.

71
00:03:34,867 --> 00:03:39,067
The link to install it is in the description.

72
00:03:39,067 --> 00:03:40,517
Come and start a topic.

